{"a_more_direct_propagation_of_information": "A more direct propagation of information refers to the efficient and streamlined transmission of data and gradients between layers within a neural network. This directness helps in reducing issues like vanishing gradients and supports better learning, particularly in complex, deeper architectures."},
{"densenet_121_s_connectivity_pattern__mitigates__challenges_related_to_vanishing_gradients": "The term \"mitigates\" in this context means that DenseNet-121\u2019s connectivity pattern helps to reduce or lessen the severity of certain issues. Specifically, it addresses problems that arise during the training of deep neural networks."},
{"challenges_related_to_vanishing_gradients": "Challenges related to vanishing gradients are common issues in training deep neural networks. They occur when the gradients used in backpropagation become very small, making it difficult for the network to learn effectively. These challenges can hinder the performance of the network, especially in deeper architectures."},
