{"accuracy": "Accuracy is one of the evaluation metrics used to measure the performance of models. It represents the proportion of correct predictions (both true positives and true negatives) among the total number of cases examined."},
{"evaluation_metrics__include__precision": "The predicate \"include\" signifies that Precision is one of the several metrics being utilized to evaluate the performance of the models. It highlights the comprehensive nature of the evaluation process, which considers multiple aspects of model performance."},
{"precision": "Precision is a metric that measures the accuracy of positive predictions made by a model. It is the ratio of true positive predictions to the total number of positive predictions (true positives plus false positives). High precision indicates that the model has a low false positive rate."},
