{"fusion": "Fusion refers to the process of combining information from different sources or modalities, such as images and text, to create a more comprehensive understanding. In the context of machine learning and data analysis, fusion techniques aim to integrate various data types to enhance the overall interpretation and decision-making capabilities of a model.|Here is another description: Fusion refers to the process of combining information from different sources or modalities to create a more comprehensive understanding. In the context of intermediary feature fusion, it involves integrating data from image and text domains to enhance the model's perception and interpretation of the situation."},
