{"limitations_owing_to_the_ambiguous_or_incomplete_information_in_any_individual_modality": "Limitations owing to the ambiguous or incomplete information in any individual modality refer to the constraints and inaccuracies that arise when information from a single source is unclear or insufficient. These limitations can hinder the model's ability to fully understand and interpret the situation accurately."},
{"proposed_approach__is_effective_in__capturing_detailed_dependencies_within_and_between_different_modalities": "The phrase \"is effective in\" indicates that the proposed approach has been demonstrated to perform well or yield positive results in a specific context or application. It highlights the approach's capability and success in achieving its intended purpose."},
{"capturing_detailed_dependencies_within_and_between_different_modalities": "Capturing detailed dependencies within and between different modalities involves the ability of the proposed approach to recognize and utilize intricate relationships and interactions among various types of data. This capability allows for a more comprehensive and nuanced understanding of the multimodal data, leading to more accurate and informed decisions."},
{"proposed_approach__enables__more_informed_decisions_especially_in_disaster_assessment_tasks": "The predicate \"enables\" signifies that the proposed approach provides the capability or means to achieve a certain outcome. In this context, it indicates that the approach facilitates a higher level of performance or effectiveness in making decisions."},
{"more_informed_decisions_especially_in_disaster_assessment_tasks": "More informed decisions, especially in disaster assessment tasks, refer to the enhanced quality and accuracy of judgments made using the proposed approach. These decisions are based on a richer and more nuanced understanding of multimodal data, leading to better outcomes in critical situations like disaster assessment."},
{"proposed_intermediate_fusion": "The proposed intermediate fusion is a method designed to integrate different modalities at a specific stage in the processing pipeline, aiming to capture detailed dependencies and interactions between them."},
