{"multimodal_fusion_methodologies": "Multimodal fusion methodologies refer to techniques that integrate and analyze data from multiple sources or modalities, such as text and images, to provide a more comprehensive understanding of a situation. In the context of disaster assessment, these methodologies leverage various types of information to enhance the accuracy and reliability of the analysis.|Here is another description: Multimodal fusion methodologies refer to techniques that integrate and analyze data from multiple sources or modalities, such as text and images, to provide a more comprehensive understanding of a situation. In the context of disaster assessment, these methodologies leverage various types of information to enhance the accuracy and effectiveness of analyses."},
