{"deep_learning_classifiers__were_prone_to__catastrophic_forgetting_during_knowledge_transfer": "The phrase \"were prone to\" indicates a tendency or susceptibility of the deep learning classifiers to exhibit a specific behavior or issue. In this context, it highlights a challenge faced by these classifiers during the process of knowledge transfer."},
{"catastrophic_forgetting_during_knowledge_transfer": "Catastrophic forgetting during knowledge transfer refers to a phenomenon where a deep learning model, after being trained on a new task, forgets previously learned information. This can significantly degrade the model's performance on earlier tasks, making it a critical issue in incremental and continual learning scenarios."},
