{"unimodal_and_multimodal_approaches": "Unimodal and multimodal approaches are methods used in disaster assessment that rely on either a single type of data (unimodal) or multiple types of data (multimodal). These approaches aim to improve the accuracy and effectiveness of disaster assessment by leveraging different sources of information.|Here is another description: Unimodal and multimodal approaches refer to different methods or techniques that utilize either a single type of data or multiple types of data, respectively. These approaches are designed to analyze and interpret information in various formats to achieve a specific goal."},
