{"informativeness": "Informativeness is a classification criterion used to evaluate the content of information, particularly in the context of disaster communication. It helps in determining the relevance and usefulness of the information provided during a disaster.|Here is another description: Informativeness is a criterion or metric used to evaluate the performance of models in task 1(a), indicating how well the model conveys or extracts meaningful information."},
