{"humanitarian_categories": "Humanitarian Categories refer to the classification system used to organize and prioritize various aspects of humanitarian efforts and responses. These categories help in assessing the needs and impacts of humanitarian crises.|Here is another description: Humanitarian Categories refer to the various classifications used to assess and address the needs of individuals affected by disasters or crises. These categories help in organizing and prioritizing aid and support efforts.|Here is another description: Humanitarian Categories refer to a classification system used to categorize various aspects of humanitarian efforts and impacts, including affected individuals, infrastructure damage, and rescue efforts.|Here is another description: Humanitarian Categories refer to a classification system used to categorize various aspects of humanitarian crises, including affected individuals, infrastructure damage, and rescue efforts.|Here is another description: Humanitarian Categories refer to the various classifications used to organize and understand the different aspects of humanitarian efforts and responses. These categories help in assessing and addressing the needs of affected populations and areas.|Here is another description: \"Humanitarian Categories\" represents the classification under which Abavisani et al.'s work is grouped. This object indicates that the study or analysis conducted by Abavisani et al. falls within the domain of humanitarian efforts, possibly involving categories related to aid, relief, or other humanitarian actions."},
{"humanitarian_categories__includes__affected_individuals": "The relation \"includes\" signifies that Humanitarian Categories encompass or contain specific elements within their scope. This predicate helps in understanding the comprehensive nature of the categories by listing what they cover."},
{"affected_individuals": "Affected individuals are people who have been impacted by a humanitarian crisis, such as natural disasters, conflicts, or other emergencies. They require assistance and support to meet their basic needs and recover from the crisis."},
{"humanitarian_categories__includes__infrastructure_and_utility_damage": "The relation \"includes\" signifies that the Humanitarian Categories encompass or contain specific elements or aspects within their scope. This predicate helps in understanding the comprehensive nature of the categories."},
{"infrastructure_and_utility_damage": "Infrastructure and utility damage refers to the harm or destruction inflicted upon essential services and facilities such as roads, bridges, water supply systems, and electricity grids. This type of damage is critical in assessing the overall impact of a disaster on a community."},
{"humanitarian_categories__includes__not_humanitarian": "The relation \"includes\" signifies that the Humanitarian Categories encompass a range of elements, one of which is explicitly labeled as \"Not humanitarian.\""},
{"not_humanitarian": "\"Not humanitarian\" within the Humanitarian Categories denotes elements or aspects that do not fall under the typical humanitarian concerns, such as direct aid or damage assessment, but are still relevant to the overall context."},
