{"other_relevant_information": "\"Other relevant information\" within the Humanitarian Categories denotes any additional data or details that are pertinent to understanding the full scope of a humanitarian situation but do not fit into the predefined categories."},
{"humanitarian_categories__includes__rescue_volunteering_or_donation_effort": "The relation \"includes\" signifies that the Humanitarian Categories encompass or contain specific types of efforts or activities that are part of humanitarian responses. This predicate helps in understanding the scope and components of humanitarian actions."},
{"rescue_volunteering_or_donation_effort": "Rescue, volunteering, or donation effort represents specific types of humanitarian activities. These efforts involve direct actions to save lives, provide support through volunteer work, or contribute resources and funds to aid those in need during crises or disasters."},
{"damage_severity_assessment": "Damage Severity Assessment is a method used to evaluate the extent of damage in various scenarios, such as natural disasters or conflicts. It categorizes the severity of impact on infrastructure, utilities, and affected individuals, helping to determine necessary repairs or interventions for restoration."},
