{"visual_transformer_vit": "Visual Transformer (ViT) is a type of neural network architecture designed for processing visual data. It has shown higher performance in certain tasks compared to traditional convolutional neural networks (CNNs), making it a preferred choice in applications requiring effective feature extraction and classification.|Here is another description: Visual Transformer (ViT) is a type of neural network architecture designed for processing visual data. It differs from traditional convolutional neural networks (CNNs) by treating image processing as a sequence-to-sequence problem, similar to how transformers handle text in natural language processing."},
