{"cnn_architectures": "CNN architectures, such as ResNet and DenseNet, are traditional neural network models widely used for image processing and classification tasks. They are known for their effectiveness in extracting features from images but, in this context, are outperformed by Visual Transformer, leading to its selection for the task at hand.|Here is another description: CNN architectures refer to convolutional neural network designs that are commonly used for image processing and feature extraction tasks. These architectures are known for their ability to automatically and adaptively learn spatial hierarchies of features from input images."},
