{"transformer_based_architectures": "Transformer-based architectures refer to a class of machine learning models that utilize the Transformer mechanism, which is designed to handle sequential data by considering the relationships between all elements in the sequence. Examples of such architectures include RoBERTa for text and Vision Transformer for images, which were employed in the study to process and understand complex data inputs."},
{"transformer_based_architectures__showed_a_tendency_to_overfit__during_the_study": "The phrase \"showed a tendency to overfit\" describes a common issue in machine learning where a model performs well on the training data but fails to generalize to new, unseen data. This occurs when the model captures noise and random fluctuations in the training data as if they were true underlying patterns."},
{"during_the_study": "\"During the study\" refers to the period when the research was conducted, involving the training and evaluation of Transformer-based architectures. This phase included experimenting with different configurations and hyperparameters to optimize model performance and address issues like overfitting."},
