{"catastrophic_forgetting_during_knowledge_transfer": "Catastrophic forgetting during knowledge transfer refers to a phenomenon where a machine learning model, after being trained on a new task, forgets the knowledge it previously acquired from earlier tasks. This issue is particularly problematic in incremental learning scenarios where the model needs to continually adapt to new information without losing its previously learned capabilities."},
{"learning_rates_regularization_and_other_hyperparameters": "The subject refers to the various hyperparameters that were adjusted during the research to improve model performance. These include learning rates, which determine the step size at each iteration while moving toward a minimum of a loss function, regularization techniques that help prevent overfitting by adding a penalty to the loss function, and other unspecified hyperparameters that influence the behavior of the model."},
