{"t_sne": "t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) is a machine learning algorithm used for dimensionality reduction. It is particularly effective at preserving the local structure of high-dimensional data when projecting it into a lower-dimensional space, typically two or three dimensions."},
{"t_sne__can_be_employed_to__validate_inconsistencies_in_the_data": "The phrase \"can be employed to\" indicates a potential use or application of t-SNE. In this context, it suggests that t-SNE has the capability or function to serve a specific purpose related to data analysis."},
{"validate_inconsistencies_in_the_data": "Validating inconsistencies in the data refers to the process of identifying and confirming discrepancies or errors within a dataset. This is crucial for ensuring data quality and reliability, especially in machine learning and data analysis tasks where accurate data is essential for model performance.|Here is another description: Validating inconsistencies in the data refers to the process of checking and confirming whether there are any discrepancies or errors within the dataset. This is crucial for ensuring the quality and reliability of the data, especially in machine learning and data analysis tasks where accurate data is essential for model performance."},
