{"future_research__could_explore__incorporating_privacy_metrics_such_as_ensuring_the_anonymity_of_users_involved_in_accidents_during_disasters": "Could explore indicates a potential area of investigation or a possible direction for future studies. In the context of disaster research, this predicate suggests that there are opportunities to delve into new methods and strategies that could improve the effectiveness and ethical considerations of disaster assessment models."},
{"incorporating_privacy_metrics_such_as_ensuring_the_anonymity_of_users_involved_in_accidents_during_disasters": "Incorporating privacy metrics, such as ensuring the anonymity of users involved in accidents during disasters, involves implementing measures to protect the personal information and identities of individuals affected by disasters. This object highlights the importance of maintaining user privacy and data security in the development and application of disaster assessment technologies."},
{"future_research__can_investigate__more_intricate_multimodal_fusion_methods_such_as_hierarchical_structures_hybrid_architectures_and_improved_attention_processes_43_45_that_mainly_improve_image_topic_representations": "\"Can investigate\" signifies the potential for future research to explore and examine new methods and techniques. In this context, it indicates that future research has the opportunity to delve into more complex and advanced multimodal fusion methods to improve the integration of textual and visual elements in disaster assessments."},
{"more_intricate_multimodal_fusion_methods_such_as_hierarchical_structures_hybrid_architectures_and_improved_attention_processes_43_45_that_mainly_improve_image_topic_representations": "More intricate multimodal fusion methods, such as hierarchical structures, hybrid architectures, and improved attention processes [43\u201345], refer to advanced techniques aimed at better integrating and analyzing multiple types of data (e.g., text and images) to enhance representations of image topics. These methods are designed to improve the accuracy of disaster assessments by more effectively combining different data modalities."},
