{"future_research__can_commission__weakly_supervised_and_semi_supervised_learning_strategies": "Can commission indicates the potential for future research to initiate, authorize, or undertake specific strategies or methods, such as adopting new learning techniques to enhance model performance and reduce reliance on labeled data."},
{"weakly_supervised_and_semi_supervised_learning_strategies": "Weakly supervised and semi-supervised learning strategies are methods that utilize a limited amount of labeled data along with a larger pool of unlabeled data to train machine learning models. These strategies aim to improve model performance and generalizability by effectively leveraging both labeled and unlabeled datasets.|Here is another description: Weakly supervised and semi-supervised learning strategies refer to methods that utilize a limited amount of labeled data along with a larger pool of unlabeled data to train machine learning models. These strategies aim to improve model performance by leveraging both labeled and unlabeled data effectively.|Here is another description: Weakly supervised and semi-supervised learning strategies refer to methods that utilize a combination of labeled and unlabeled data to train machine learning models. These strategies aim to leverage the vast amount of unlabeled data available, especially in domains like social media, to enhance model performance without heavily relying on manually labeled datasets."},
{"weakly_supervised_and_semi_supervised_learning_strategies__can_take_advantage_of__the_wealth_of_unlabeled_social_media_data_and_label_them": "The phrase \"can take advantage of\" indicates that weakly supervised and semi-supervised learning strategies have the capability to utilize and benefit from a specific resource or dataset. In this context, it means these strategies can effectively use the available data to enhance model training and performance."},
